   "notes": "Fisher House (Catholic Chaplaincy, the former Black Swan inn), Guildhall Street front: jettied first floor of white render over a ground floor of buff gault brick; black fascia/bressumer with brackets along the jetty; three arched-head sash windows above; ground floor three leaded casements (wide one in the middle), red-brick arched doorway with plank door and a small window to its right; old tile roof with three gabled dormers and modillion eaves. From Mapillary 738114823524885 and the Commons photo (CC BY-SA 4.0). Fitted to the 7.5 m OSM wall, so spacings are compressed slightly."
